<$ss.hero title="Slipstream UI Primitives" subtitle="Reusable wikitext widgets for building responsive dashboards, hubs, and interactive layouts."/>

Slipstream ships with a suite of lightweight, responsive UI primitives implemented in `$:/plugins/mblackman/slipstream/widgets/ui-primitives`. These widgets follow modern TiddlyWiki v5.4.0+ custom widget standards and render cleanly across desktop, tablet, and mobile screens.

---

! 1. Hero Banner (`<$ss.hero>`)

The hero widget renders a visually prominent header block with an optional title, subtitle, and action buttons.

!! Live Example

<$ss.hero title="Project Workspace" subtitle="Organize ideas, capture notes, and track your creative projects."/>

!! Wikitext Syntax

```wikitext
<$ss.hero
  title="Project Workspace"
  subtitle="Organize ideas, capture notes, and track your creative projects."
/>
```

---

! 2. Responsive Card Grid (`<$ss.grid>`)

The grid widget arranges cards or content blocks into a CSS Grid with automatic wrapping (`repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min, 1fr))`).

* ''`min`'' (default `240px`): The minimum width of each column before wrapping.
* ''`gap`'' (default `16px`): The gap spacing between grid items.

!! Live Example

<$ss.grid min="220px">
  <$ss.card badge="Alpha" accent="#3b82f6">
    <h4>Component 1</h4>
    <p>Adaptive layout sizing.</p>
  </$ss.card>
  <$ss.card badge="Beta" accent="#10b981">
    <h4>Component 2</h4>
    <p>Flexible column flow.</p>
  </$ss.card>
  <$ss.card badge="Gamma" accent="#f59e0b">
    <h4>Component 3</h4>
    <p>Mobile-ready auto-wrap.</p>
  </$ss.card>
</$ss.grid>

!! Wikitext Syntax

```wikitext
<$ss.grid min="220px">
  <$ss.card badge="Alpha" accent="#3b82f6">
    <h4>Component 1</h4>
    <p>Adaptive layout sizing.</p>
  </$ss.card>
  ...
</$ss.grid>
```

---

! 3. Content Card (`<$ss.card>`)

Cards provide a container with subtle border, background tint, rounded corners, and hover elevation.

* ''`badge`'' (optional): Text displayed in an upper-right badge pill.
* ''`accent`'' (optional): CSS color applied to the card's accent border.

!! Live Example

<$ss.card badge="Interactive" accent="var(--tpc-primary)">
<h3>Custom Information Card</h3>
<p>Cards accept any valid wikitext inside, including links, lists, or transcluded content.</p>
<$ss.progress value="80" total="100" label="Resource Utilization"/>
</$ss.card>

---

! 4. Property Pill (`<$ss.prop-pill>`)

Renders a two-part key/value badge. Used automatically by the `ObjectPropertyHeader` beneath tiddler titles, but can also be used anywhere in your notes.

!! Live Example

<$ss.prop-pill name="Status" value="In Progress"/>
<$ss.prop-pill name="Priority" value="High"/>
<$ss.prop-pill name="Version" value="v1.2.0"/>

!! Wikitext Syntax

```wikitext
<$ss.prop-pill name="Status" value="In Progress"/>
<$ss.prop-pill name="Priority" value="High"/>
<$ss.prop-pill name="Version" value="v1.2.0"/>
```

---

! 5. Progress Bar (`<$ss.progress>`)

Renders a smooth progress bar with percentage computation and optional label.

* ''`value`'': Current numeric value (e.g. `12`).
* ''`total`'' (default `100`): Maximum numeric value (e.g. `15`).
* ''`label`'' (optional): Descriptive label displayed above the bar.

!! Live Example

<$ss.progress value="6" total="10" label="Milestone Completion (6 / 10)"/>

<div style="height: 12px;"></div>

<$ss.progress value="95" total="100" label="Code Coverage"/>

!! Wikitext Syntax

```wikitext
<$ss.progress value="6" total="10" label="Milestone Completion (6 / 10)"/>
<$ss.progress value="95" total="100" label="Code Coverage"/>
```

